[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Ground Alias Admission Boundary

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-GROUND-ALIAS-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Bind qualified ground aliases and refuse unqualified contexts
STATEMENT: >>>
Selected preparation shall either bind active case-insensitive exact gnd node references under a qualified explicit policy or atomically refuse unqualified contexts with a structured unsupported_ground diagnostic. It shall not allocate an automatically grounded alias as a floating unknown, fabricate a grounding source, publish a partial request or remove a failed observable merely to obtain agreement. Literal node zero remains ground. Unused bodies and declarations without an active reference shall remain inert.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The frozen f64edbd corpus incorrectly admitted rc-meas-ac.sp and its mirror as floating circuits. The fc5db25 census used the interim unsupported_ground_alias refusal. GroundAliasPolicy and OperatingPointBridge now normalize qualified references; PreparationSemanticsTests, GroundAliasTests and GroundAliasNativeTests cover supported and refused contexts. Historical frozen classifications remain unchanged. Issue34 execution evidence is retained separately.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-GROUND-ALIAS-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Qualify dialect-aware ground normalization
STATEMENT: >>>
Before admitting gnd aliases, preparation shall qualify default native ground normalization, global and subcircuit scope, PSpice header exceptions, and explicit no-auto-ground behavior against original ngspice inputs. Automatically grounded aliases shall not become independently measured root unknowns; disabled normalization shall preserve ordinary node/port/global behavior. A grounded formal shall not allocate its ignored actual. Automatic mode shall use PSpice semantics when an active VSWITCH requires that compatibility mode. Unsupported options and unqualified nested, protected-global or delimiter contexts shall refuse rather than be silently masked.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Issue34 follow-up. Native inpcom.c inp_fix_gnd_name and search_plain_identifier were inspected; three initial native probes established default0V versus PSpice/no-auto1.5V in the same formal-ground divider. The bounded implementation reuses generated header/node/port metadata and the standard .NET nonbacktracking regex engine for the native header identifier-boundary predicate. Tight vector brackets, nested protected bodies and protected explicit global gnd contexts remain named refusals. GroundAliasNativeTests compare original OP/AC fixtures on LU/faer; The clean 26cfad9 full census completed with valid provenance:85 prepared,23 requested executions and11 native agreements among928 paths, including both original ordinary rc-meas-ac.sp paths. Evidence: evidence/issue34-ground-census.json. Broader dialect interactions remain explicitly refused; Draft status does not imply full normalization compatibility.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-GROUND-ALIAS-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Exact zero control reductions preserve physical source contracts
STATEMENT: >>>
After ground and port binding, affine behavioral terms with reference-node voltage shall contribute exactly zero without allocating auxiliary unknowns. A zero differential control shall reduce to a zero voltage constraint for voltage output or a zero current for current output, preserving original observable branch identity where defined. Introduced independent sources shall carry explicit zero AC excitation. Source amplitudes, solver tolerances and unsupported nonlinear-expression refusals shall remain unchanged.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: OperatingPointBridge.Controlled and bound affine-term filtering. Verification: zero-control RED regressions, independent current-driven E/G distinctions, native OP/AC gain/summer tests on both providers. This is exact algebraic reduction, not an approximate behavioral kernel or relaxed engine validation.
<<<
